   "id": "yoma.18a.11",
   "daf": "18a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "עֶרֶב יוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים שַׁחֲרִית וְכוּ׳. תָּנָא: אַף הַשְּׂעִירִים. וְתַנָּא דִּידַן מַאי טַעְמָא לָא תְּנָא שְׂעִירִים? כֵּיוָן דְּעַל חֵטְא קָא אָתוּ — חָלְשָׁא דַּעְתֵּיהּ.",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: «On Yom Kippur eve» in the «morning,» the elders pass different animals before the High Priest. A tanna «taught» in the Tosefta: «Even goats» were brought before him. The Gemara asks: «And the tanna» of «our» mishna, «what is the reason» that «he did not teach» that «goats» were among the animals that passed before the High Priest? The Gemara answers: «Since» goats «come» as atonement «for sins,» passing them before the High Priest will evoke transgressions and he will «become distraught.»"
  }
 ],
